    perf: scope node fixtures to the layers they assert — selftest 2.49 s -> 1.58 s CPU (PERF-013)
    
    tests/selftest.sh invoked scripts/project-node.sh 13 times and paid every layer for
    fixtures that assert one layer's row. Before (perf lane tick
    code-factory-perf-2026-11-03-14-51-11 at d5f7fb2): 2.58 / 2.49 / 2.49 s user+sys, 34 PASS,
    loadavg ~4.9; re-measured in this worktree at d5f7fb2 as 2.50 / 2.45 / 2.45 s CPU.
    ~85% of that was layer work no fixture asserts.
    
    scripts/project-node.sh gains --layers <list> (comma-separated subset of 00,10,20,30,40;
    single value = list of one):
      - validated before any layer runs: empty list, unknown element or stray comma prints the
        usage line to stderr and exits 2 with no [00] row;
      - prints one "SCOPE: layers <list> (fixture mode — not a node certification)" line before
        layer 00 and "  SKIP  layer NN (out of scope)" where each skipped layer would have run;
      - never writes $HOME/.node/node.json, even under --apply with every in-scope layer green —
        layer 90 prints "  SKIP  layer 90 (fixture mode: no manifest)" instead (N-4 by
        construction); a scope without 00 does not resolve the disk floor (nothing consumes it);
      - summary line keeps its shape (NODE: PASS / NODE: FAIL (n)).
    Unscoped runs are byte-identical: same rows, same order, same manifest, same exit codes
    (verified by diffing HEAD's script against the new one over 10 fixtures + 3 argument-error
    surfaces; only the script path, bash "line N" diagnostics and the extended usage line differ).
    specs/NODE.md documents the surface and what a scoped run may not do.
    
    Fixtures moved to the minimal layer set they assert:
      §3 unreachable crier -> --layers 00; §4 missing ref, §4 private-repo arm, §4b resolved-ref
      -> --layers 40; §14 red+green adapter arms -> --layers 20; §15 bus-vs-clone masking arm
      -> --layers 30,40 (it needs the clone to succeed and the bus to fail).
    Every assertion kept its exact grep -Fxc string and rc expectation; no assertion was
    redesigned. Left unscoped: §15's two documented-shape arms (they run the documented command
    as written), §2 empty PATH (whole-checker property, measured 0.00 s), §13 malformed floor
    (exits before any layer runs).
    
    After: 1.63 / 1.56 / 1.55 s user+sys (real 1.69 / 1.59 / 1.55), rc=0, 34 PASS rows each,
    SELFTEST: PASS — mean 2.47 -> 1.58 s CPU (-36%). The <1.2 s target is not met and is not
    reachable by fixture scoping under this brief: the two documented-shape arms cost 0.28 s,
    the two python suites outside this diff 0.25 s, §3's layer-00 run 0.09 s (floor resolver
    spawns three python3), and ~0.8 s is non-node gate work. A throwaway copy that also scoped
    the documented arms measured 1.19-1.24 s CPU — the technique's ceiling, and it would no
    longer run the documented command.
    
